    {
      "path": "std::borrow::Borrow",
      "kind": "trait",
      "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.Borrow.html",
      "score": 64.3,
      "docs": [
        {
          "type": "truncatedBlock",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A trait for borrowing data.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "In Rust, it is common to provide different representations of a type for",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "different use cases. For instance, storage location and management for a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "value can be specifically chosen as appropriate for a particular use via",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "pointer types such as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Box<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fboxed%2Fstruct%2EBox"
                },
                {
                  "text": " or ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Rc<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Frc%2Fstruct%2ERc"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". Beyond these generic",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "wrappers that can be used with any type, some types provide optional",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "facets providing potentially costly functionality. An example for such a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "type is ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fstring%2Fstruct%2EString"
                },
                {
                  "text": " which adds the ability to extend a string to the basic",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "str",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/primitive.str.html"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". This requires keeping additional information unnecessary for a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "simple, immutable string.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "These types provide access to the underlying data through references",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "to the type of that data. They are said to be ‘borrowed as’ that type.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "For instance, a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Box<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fboxed%2Fstruct%2EBox"
                },
                {
                  "text": " can be borrowed as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " while a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fstring%2Fstruct%2EString"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be borrowed as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "str",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Types express that they can be borrowed as some type ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " by implementing",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Borrow<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", providing a reference to a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " in the trait’s",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "borrow",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                },
                {
                  "text": " method. A type is free to borrow as several different types.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "If it wishes to mutably borrow as the type, allowing the underlying data",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "to be modified, it can additionally implement ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "BorrowMut<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/borrow/trait.BorrowMut.html"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Further, when providing implementations for additional traits, it needs",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "to be considered whether they should behave identically to those of the",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "underlying type as a consequence of acting as a representation of that",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "underlying type. Generic code typically uses ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Borrow<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " when it relies",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "on the identical behavior of these additional trait implementations.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "These traits will likely appear as additional trait bounds.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "In particular ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Eq",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Ord",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " and ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Hash",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " must be equivalent for",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "borrowed and owned values: ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "x.borrow() == y.borrow()",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " should give the",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "same result as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "x == y",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "If generic code merely needs to work for all types that can",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "provide a reference to related type ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", it is often better to use",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "AsRef<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/convert/trait.AsRef.html"
                },
                {
                  "text": " as more types can safely implement it.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "level": "Title",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Examples",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "As a data collection, ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "HashMap<K, V>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fcollections%2Fstruct%2EHashMap"
                },
                {
                  "text": " owns both keys and values. If",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "the key’s actual data is wrapped in a managing type of some kind, it",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "should, however, still be possible to search for a value using a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "reference to the key’s data. For instance, if the key is a string, then",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "it is likely stored with the hash map as a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fstring%2Fstruct%2EString"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", while it should",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "be possible to search using a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "&str",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/primitive.str.html"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". Thus, ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "insert",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " needs to",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "operate on a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " while ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "get",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " needs to be able to use a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "&str",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Slightly simplified, the relevant parts of ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "HashMap<K, V>",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " look like",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "this:",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "codeBlock",
              "lang": "rust",
              "code": "use std::borrow::Borrow;\nuse std::hash::Hash;\n\npub struct HashMap<K, V> {\n    // fields omitted\n}\n\nimpl<K, V> HashMap<K, V> {\n    pub fn insert(&self, key: K, value: V) -> Option<V>\n    where K: Hash + Eq\n    {\n        // ...\n    }\n\n    pub fn get<Q>(&self, k: &Q) -> Option<&V>\n    where\n        K: Borrow<Q>,\n        Q: Hash + Eq + ?Sized\n    {\n        // ...\n    }\n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "The entire hash map is generic over a key type ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "K",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". Because these keys",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "are stored with the hash map, this type has to own the key’s data.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "When inserting a key-value pair, the map is given such a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "K",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " and needs",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "to find the correct hash bucket and check if the key is already present",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "based on that ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "K",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". It therefore requires ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "K: Hash + Eq",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "When searching for a value in the map, however, having to provide a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "reference to a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "K",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " as the key to search for would require to always",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "create such an owned value. For string keys, this would mean a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
