      "score": 64.0,
      "docs": [
        {
          "type": "truncatedBlock",
          "nodes": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "A trait for borrowing data.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "In Rust, it is common to provide different representations of a type for",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "different use cases. For instance, storage location and management for a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "value can be specifically chosen as appropriate for a particular use via",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "pointer types such as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Box<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fboxed%2Fstruct%2EBox"
                },
                {
                  "text": " or ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Rc<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Frc%2Fstruct%2ERc"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". Beyond these generic",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "wrappers that can be used with any type, some types provide optional",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "facets providing potentially costly functionality. An example for such a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "type is ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fstring%2Fstruct%2EString"
                },
                {
                  "text": " which adds the ability to extend a string to the basic",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "str",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/primitive.str.html"
                },
                {
                  "text": ". This requires keeping additional information unnecessary for a",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "simple, immutable string.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "These types provide access to the underlying data through references",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "to the type of that data. They are said to be ‘borrowed as’ that type.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "For instance, a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Box<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fboxed%2Fstruct%2EBox"
                },
                {
                  "text": " can be borrowed as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " while a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "String",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/index.html?search=core%3A%3A%2E%2F%2E%2E%2Fstd%2Fstring%2Fstruct%2EString"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be borrowed as ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "str",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ".",
                  "style": "Plain"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "text": "Types express that they can be borrowed as some type ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " by implementing",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Borrow<T>",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": ", providing a reference to a ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "T",
                  "style": "InlineCode"
                },
                {
                  "text": " in the trait’s",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "borrow",
                  "style": "InlineCode",
                  "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/"
                },
                {
                  "text": " method. A type is free to borrow as several different types.",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": " ",
                  "style": "Plain"
                },
                {
                  "text": "If it wishes to mutably borrow as the type, allowing the underlying data",
